WEBVTT

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.460
I... I ended up coming 
all the way to Hawaii!

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.460
Aloha!

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.930
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.420
Wave 10

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.730
You decided to come so suddenly, 
I was shocked, Corgi.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.310
I mean, we're shocked, too!

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.640
It really was sudden.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.640
Let's go do some intensive training.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.900
I'm in!

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:56.370
Then, starting today, will you entrust me 
with a week of your time?

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.860
Starting... today?

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.530
This conversation 
is moving pretty fast, Bill.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.790
Well, I did make the plans quickly.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:07.750
I want all our young surfers 
to work toward leveling up,

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.290
so I hope you'll all participate.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.850
Well, we've got no reason to say no.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:13.830
That's right.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.800
But what kind of intensive training?

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.090
I'll explain when we get there.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.670
Now, let's go.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:23.430
That's how it happened.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.230
It was so sudden, I only got 
stuff ready for surfing...

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.680
Is that okay?

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.500
I've already finished 
preparations on this end.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:36.640
Will I be able to watch <i>Miruru</i> 
in real time in Honolulu?

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.190
I'll make arrangements immediately.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:42.820
Bringing Masaki and the others 
all the way here... Mahalo, Bill.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.390
I should be the one thanking you.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.950
I'm honored that you'll be participating 
in the training, Tanaka-kun.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.780
So, this is the Duke Kahanamoku statue?

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.210
Is he someone famous?

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:59.280
Masaki... You don't know 
who Duke Kahanamoku is?

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.470
No, I don't.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.430
Neither do I.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:03.470
Seriously, you two...

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.160
At the beginning of the 20th century,

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:11.040
surfing was still only being 
practiced in a few places.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:19.030
Duke appeared in the 1912 
Stockholm Olympics as a swimmer

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.410
and set a world record.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.990
After that, he was invited to swimming 
competitions all over the world.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:29.850
And everywhere he went, 
he gave a surfing demonstration.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.750
Which means...

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.310
Duke is the one who spread 
surfing all over the world!

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:39.240
So he was someone 
that was like Aruru is to Miruru.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:45.080
Without him, we wouldn't be here 
the way we are now.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:49.390
Thank you, Duke.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.790
So, what are we doing next?

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.960
First, some sightseeing around Honolulu.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.470
After everyone's enjoyed 
themselves to the fullest,

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.780
we'll head to the North Shore.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.760
North Shore?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:09.410
Yes. It's a place where big waves 
come in. A mecca for surfers!

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:12.040
A pilgrimage...

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:16.040
Winter is the best season, 
so you can expect good things.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:16.780
Okay!

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.530
That gets me fired up.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.130
<i>Hinaoka Sakura

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.920
Hey. Looks like everyone's doing good.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.490
Why is Tadao-san in Oarai?

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:31.510
Isokichi and Hammer have 
something good going,

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.900
so he went to chaperone a date.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.070
<i>"What? Hawaii?"</i>

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.730
<i>"Tanaka-kun looks like 
he's doing well. I'm glad."</i>

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:41.270
<i>"I'm so jealous! Buy me 
lots of souvenirs, okay?"</i>

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.070
<i>"Lots!"</i>

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.660
L-Lots...

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.940
Don't worry. I know some good shops.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:51.950
Well, then. Let's get ourselves in order 
while we do some sightseeing.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:57.580
Okay, ohana. Follow me!

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.870
All of these are aloha shirts?

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:04.840
It's overwhelming.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.570
In Hawaii, aloha shirts are formal wear.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:10.320
Owning one is sure to prove useful.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.100
Okay, time for a fashion show!

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.290
Ta-dah! What do you think?

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.100
Oh, a surfing pattern.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.740
This board design... It's very nice.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.140
Right? The line here...

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:25.230
Don't discuss the design 
of a board on an aloha shirt.

00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:27.460
Sea turtles!

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.790
They're called "honu" in Hawaii.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:32.490
They bring happiness 
as guardian spirits of the sea.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:42.250
Honu, honu, honu. Honu, honu, honu.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.720
I sort of didn't expect you 
to pick a flower pattern.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.550
The hibiscus is considered 
a very dignified pattern.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.250
It seems like something I would be able to 
wear to important family ceremonies.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.650
That's very rational reasoning.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.510
Oh! A Japanese print!

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.720
So, they have aloha shirts like this too!

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:51.690
You can really feel the connection 
between Japan and Hawaii.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:54.010
I found one! I found Miruru!

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.430
They even have prints like this?

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:01.160
Can I have a turkey club panini?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:07.040
Can I have a spinach and egg...

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.720
Hey, your English seems worse than usual.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.000
What a fascinating phenomenon.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:15.660
Everything here at this shop is exquisite.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.160
I wonder if they have any 
dried sweet potato ice cream.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.520
Can I buy some mixed fruit?

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.920
Sure! Let's all share it.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.430
It's good!

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.810
It tastes like I'm in a foreign country!

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:40.180
I think I get what you're saying.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.510
Wh-What's wrong?

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:51.800
A deliciousness that robs one of words...

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:55.450
The first time I ate some, 
it was a shock for me, too.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.630
Southern islands do have fruit 
associated with their image,

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:00.950
but you'd never think the flavor
difference would be this huge.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.830
Yeah. I was shocked.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:03.900
And...

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.880
even the air feels different from Japan.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.040
Yeah. The air is so clear and peaceful.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.330
This is so good!

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.820
You've gotta eat malasadas freshly fried.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.790
I can't get enough 
of these custard-filled ones!

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:34.210
I didn't expect you 
to love sweets this much.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.340
Hey, Tanaka!

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.890
Aloha!

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:43.480
Yeah.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:45.350
Yeah.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:49.510
You weren't in the water, 
so I got a little worried.

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:51.220
What are you up to?

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:55.020
My friends are visiting from Japan 
and I'm showing them around.

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:56.540
For real? Cool!

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.280
They're all surfers.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.620
All good enough to perform internationally.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.170
That's awesome, man!

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:03.760
Aloha!

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.620
Aloha!

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.500
Have a nice trip, boys!

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.930
A hui hou!

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:13.560
You've gotten super good at English!

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.980
You're just Tanaka. How dare you?

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.700
They're friends from high 
school. Mike and Kalani.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.510
And they're amazing surfers.

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:24.770
I...

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:27.900
I'm really glad I came to Hawaii.

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:32.480
Corgi, you said it earlier, didn't you?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.650
The air feels different in Hawaii.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.900
When I'm here in this space... 
How can I put it...

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.030
I can stay positive.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:48.980
There are waves, and I am here.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:53.130
It makes me feel like that's enough.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:01.260
Holo i mua! It's time to charge forward!

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.310
Miruru!

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:17.810
I heard that climbing Diamond 
Head feels like a nice walk, but...

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:19.240
This is rough.

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:25.600
Who knew a place this wonderful existed?

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.630
Oh. It's started to rain.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:33.350
It doesn't look like there's any shelter 
for us to wait it out in.

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:34.720
Should we go back?

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:38.710
Don't worry. Hawaii's 
weather changes quickly.

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:42.300
You said not to worry!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.290
A man who looks good dripping wet 
is a handsome man. Like you, Naoya.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:48.600
It might actually be a good thing.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:51.100
When it rains...

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:52.370
Huh?

00:11:58.240 --> 00:11:59.610
Wow!

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:00.900
A rainbow!

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.010
Hey... There're two!

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:05.620
Oh, it's a double rainbow.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:11.910
This view is incredible.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.660
It really is.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:17.250
No rain, no rainbow.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:20.660
It's a saying here in Hawaii.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:23.560
If it doesn't rain, there 
will never be rainbows.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:26.350
After difficult things, sad things,

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:29.510
happiness is waiting. 
That's what the saying means.

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:34.020
I see...

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:39.420
It's like you said, Bill. 
I'm glad it rained.

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:42.490
A double rainbow.

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:56.360
Wow!

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:02.050
Please, think of this like your 
own home, and feel free to relax.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.980
They're all the newest models!

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:26.110
<i>Ru... Rururururu... Miruru... Mirurururu...</i>

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:26.690
Miruru! Miruru! Miruru!

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.860
<i>Miruru!</i>

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:32.530
Collection?

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:36.330
Yes. I really wanted to show everyone.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.400
I'm sure you'll like it.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.990
Don't be too surprised yet.

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:59.210
Seriously?

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.270
Wow!

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:04.020
How many are there?

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:09.460
When you want to loosen up, 
please feel free to use the pool.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.630
Wow!

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:19.620
A wave pool?

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.790
This is the first time 
I've seen the real thing.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:26.760
All right!

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:36.810
This is insane!

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:42.760
Corgi! I'm next!

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:45.610
These tubes don't suffer at all 
in comparison to the real thing.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.320
It's magnificent.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.450
But...

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:53.190
with the ocean so close, 
a wave pool is just sort of...

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.330
Is sushi all right for dinner?

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.480
What? Sushi? Yes!

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:06.340
That's Bill for you. 
Well, should we go out and eat?

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:08.590
Hello. Welcome back.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:10.090
What?

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:13.480
They're here! The chefs have come here!

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.290
Bill-kun, this is beyond insane!

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:20.710
This is a fish known in Hawaii as "moi."

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:23.160
Moi? I've never heard of it.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:25.120
Don't worry about it. Let's just try it!

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:33.960
It's so good!

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:38.550
They say that only royalty used 
to be allowed to eat this fish.

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:41.710
Hearing that makes it 
taste even more delicious.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:44.660
Bill is so crazy rich, it's sort of fun.

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.130
Thank you.

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:48.560
Thank you for the delicious meal!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.760
This is the best!

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.410
All the tiredness just fades away...

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:01.520
But, Bill...

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:04.820
I've been wondering, why are you 
doing all of this for us?

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.020
You could say...

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:09.780
it's all for love.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:10.930
What?

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.150
Of surfing!

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.160
Oh.

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:20.240
When you're facing the waves...

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:27.030
things like money, standing, and prestige 
are all the same... They're worthless.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:30.420
Surfing has taught me that.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.460
I am wealthy.

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:39.310
But money is simply a means 
by which to accomplish a goal.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:41.310
A goal?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:44.790
A paradigm shift through surfing.

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:47.950
This world has been swallowed up 
by the tremendous power of economics.

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:51.320
Now that it's facing an impasse, 
the power to change everything...

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:55.080
I think that power lies in surfing.

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:57.130
I see.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:59.060
What's a "paradigm shift"?

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:02.080
"Shift"... Maybe he's talking 
about part-time jobs?

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:07.580
Which means that increasing the number 
of surfers is, in itself, your goal, Bill?

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:10.200
Yes. To be precise,

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:14.590
it's those surfers who place value in surfing 
and not money that I want to increase.

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:16.970
Like all of you.

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:20.060
Hmm. By increasing the surfing population,

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:22.800
the existing value system 
can be shaken up...

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:25.600
I've never even considered that!

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:31.430
Those two seem to understand each other.

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:33.790
Yuta's switch has been tripped.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.870
This is going to take a while.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:38.400
Can I go watch <i>Miruru</i> now?

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:41.370
All right, let's leave the complicated 
conversations there.

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:44.370
Let's have a toast. To tomorrow.

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:46.630
To our training on the North Shore!

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:48.000
Yeah.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:50.700
North Shore!

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:08.140
The wind feels amazing!

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:10.260
Y-Yeah, it does.

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:12.600
Hey, are you sure about this?

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:15.190
I-I have my license.

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:17.800
In Hawaii, you can get it 
at the age of 16!

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:21.780
This is fun, isn't it, Miruru?

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:24.710
Tanaka, make sure to keep 
your eyes on the road, okay?

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:27.750
Oh, shut up! I know!

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:31.170
We should arrive soon.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:32.000
Yes.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:37.170
The entryway to the North Shore, 
a surfer's gateway to success... Haleiwa.

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:06.760
Wow...

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:08.580
Yeah...

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:18.210
It's completely different from Oarai.

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:21.510
It's true. The waves on 
the North Shore are special.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:23.630
But you know,

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:27.650
they say that the big waves you get here 
on the North Shore are born in Japan.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:29.230
Huh? In Japan?

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:32.440
The low pressure fields created 
in Japan's winter season

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:35.360
head deep into the Pacific 
and create huge waves.

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:39.900
When those swells reach the North Shore,

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:42.490
they become what we know as "big waves."

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:45.810
I see. The ocean really is all connected.

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:52.750
Hey, look at that!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:57.880
"That"? It can't be!

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.760
Fuke... Rindo?

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:12.290
I wouldn't expect anything less from him.

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:16.470
Yes. Even confronted with a 
big wave, he's riding perfectly.

00:20:16.470 --> 00:20:19.030
So he came to Hawaii, too.

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.460
A coincidence?

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:22.740
It can't be.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:25.910
Talking about special training 
all of a sudden... Was this why?

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:36.570
How is it going?

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:40.930
You're here?

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:43.760
Fuke-san! Will you surf with us?

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:45.050
What?

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:46.740
It would be a waste of time.

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:47.950
Please?

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.390
The only thing I see is the waves.

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:58.820
I have no interest in the surfing of others.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:04.450
Sorry to make such a fuss!

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.360
You really have some guts, Corgi.

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:10.700
I saw the chance, and
I couldn't help myself.

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:14.210
Why not ask that man?

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:34.730
Sho...

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:50.880
But it can't be Sho, right?

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:53.270
No one can blame you 
for making that mistake!

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:55.860
Hayamichi-san is Sho's 
big brother, after all.

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:57.250
Huh? Big brother?

00:21:57.990 --> 00:22:00.050
What? You didn't know?

00:22:00.050 --> 00:22:01.130
Huh?

00:22:01.610 --> 00:22:02.880
What?

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.760
Pleased to meet you, Masaki-kun.

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.640
Wave 11

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.640
He reminds me 
of someone...

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.640
Nalu
